[{:db/id "q-40310/selection/4bf6dd19b67f21e3d989056b85307162fae5b4b119455833dfa737e1150d56ad" :answer/id #uuid "f81a7ce8-8150-58f7-b367-ff5677a1ca87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310/selection/1966d8255529bacb489fa43aedb24b3fa9beeaaa2157768264b90df29243932a" :answer/id #uuid "82e95abf-1ce8-514e-ac39-d2d3233842d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310/selection/6bcf3a29451b5dbcb3d4a078d2d65ba9a1dfd9176f1f190b5ee291b2ce365914" :answer/id #uuid "c2ac3cb7-46cb-573c-a2c7-948943dd5c65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{224}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310/selection/a3fd14d895eea444df556fb01710d338625cbe378eee32a13b04e1c01ef871de" :answer/id #uuid "a58b7101-9984-5c33-8e83-e53f9e9cc733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{512}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310/selection/8197c4b1a16b064705559d8263ca42963ad5e2eab51fa6bc86b2f5b3ebb6e54a" :answer/id #uuid "5792f80b-6b71-580d-86ff-b05818c3fea5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{64}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3fae6b5-8536-547d-bf06-f9189c3b9375" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40310/selection/a3fd14d895eea444df556fb01710d338625cbe378eee32a13b04e1c01ef871de" :answer-field/choices ["q-40310/selection/4bf6dd19b67f21e3d989056b85307162fae5b4b119455833dfa737e1150d56ad" "q-40310/selection/1966d8255529bacb489fa43aedb24b3fa9beeaaa2157768264b90df29243932a" "q-40310/selection/6bcf3a29451b5dbcb3d4a078d2d65ba9a1dfd9176f1f190b5ee291b2ce365914" "q-40310/selection/a3fd14d895eea444df556fb01710d338625cbe378eee32a13b04e1c01ef871de" "q-40310/selection/8197c4b1a16b064705559d8263ca42963ad5e2eab51fa6bc86b2f5b3ebb6e54a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40310" :question/id #uuid "ecb72902-5e9e-57ac-8d4a-9417265e93b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40310" :question/problem "Consider the negative infinite geometric sequence that has a third term equal to $-1$ and a seventh term equal to $-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that $4\\,096={8}^{4}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{3}=-1$ and ${a}_{7}=-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-3} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{4\\,096})}{(-1)} \\\\ {r}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{4\\,096} \\\\ {r}^{4} & ={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[4]{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4}} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have taken the positive fourth root since we're told that the sequence is negative.\n\nNow, using the formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}\n$$\n\nfor the $n$th term of the geometric sequence, we can find the first term. Indeed, for $n=3$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}(\\frac{1}{64}) \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{-64}{(1-\\frac{1}{8})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{64}{(\\frac{7}{8})} \\\\  & =-64\\cdot \\frac{8}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{512}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-40310/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0adffc7-ef35-5f7a-a790-06addb354c2e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection/c522e12a66c77916a35d5fc63d6bb88726a384796b883facbe11ec56bcbdf337" :answer/id #uuid "2e0be7b3-8af8-5a9a-bb3f-de5c4c5261ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection/0b1979f0f897557b4bb0f562e951effd9bc1000e2a185f4400e878ecc4599de5" :answer/id #uuid "8301c66b-d122-5599-a107-f51d12c7ae5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection/82e31094254c29e667c03f93ab9c3001573066f41671c999c0842a89fac27032" :answer/id #uuid "4e6d32e6-6902-56e2-be2e-d3570035f1f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection/d5c0962af13acd73fe87c72b00e4ff3ad18da62358233c0fe8a3c12a411f443e" :answer/id #uuid "fc1eeffe-9811-576b-9685-b4b7de728f4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection/05ceb2495474aa339bbcef5cc707fe2df4f14c3dba4aed38fcbb0f00b735cd47" :answer/id #uuid "ae7505b0-946b-593f-8440-2f0711e82b81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "64c395fd-1562-5ab5-abca-33a09b4e9937" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75627/selection/0b1979f0f897557b4bb0f562e951effd9bc1000e2a185f4400e878ecc4599de5" :answer-field/choices ["q-75627/selection/c522e12a66c77916a35d5fc63d6bb88726a384796b883facbe11ec56bcbdf337" "q-75627/selection/0b1979f0f897557b4bb0f562e951effd9bc1000e2a185f4400e878ecc4599de5" "q-75627/selection/82e31094254c29e667c03f93ab9c3001573066f41671c999c0842a89fac27032" "q-75627/selection/d5c0962af13acd73fe87c72b00e4ff3ad18da62358233c0fe8a3c12a411f443e" "q-75627/selection/05ceb2495474aa339bbcef5cc707fe2df4f14c3dba4aed38fcbb0f00b735cd47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75627" :question/id #uuid "0713f9bb-a7f6-5623-831b-c2f55d54c8c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75627" :question/problem "Calculate the sum to infinity of the geometric series $6.4+4.8+3.6+2.7+⋯$" :question/worked-solution "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=6.4$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{4.8}{6.4}=0.75.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{1-0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{0.25} \\\\  & =25.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75627/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2954b59f-d701-502f-963b-b62098a87c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75627"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "5905f926-c972-51f0-9e2e-a72c55723a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" :answer/id #uuid "cf66df67-e273-59c0-840c-ef5de8e41bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "eba9c543-817b-5b79-8a44-90d9c83c635e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "12c6198a-3ef7-51d7-a026-7aa550165daa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "8260b390-b68b-5938-a0c5-bc0981186c5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "76697a56-01d7-5522-9541-567f8a2461b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124570/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer-field/choices ["q-124570/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-124570/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" "q-124570/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-124570/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" "q-124570/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124570" :question/id #uuid "d05dedb0-ea9f-500b-8b24-c5b96491cf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-124570" :question/problem "Consider the positive infinite geometric sequence that has a first term equal to $9$ and a third term equal to $4.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{1}=9$ and ${a}_{3}=4.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3-1} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {r}^{2} & ={(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have taken the positive square root since we're told that the sequence is positive.\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{(1-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0adffc7-ef35-5f7a-a790-06addb354c2e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347769/field-1/dd033485ad1b20e02b3b038ad4ace3793fe552208d4049b9ebad6a1f6c399e1a" :answer/id #uuid "539f08d6-5a09-5c3f-8f7c-f85d512a89eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{160}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347769/field-1/d4fc5106c86c1246cb2d77e899c8c1892c146704c468558a9a4eec5c8a74d079" :answer/id #uuid "e0522c5a-4e17-5ded-8110-b77d569c0e45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{160}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347769/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5605b1-eb69-55a5-b2ed-13c40679dc6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347769/field-1/dd033485ad1b20e02b3b038ad4ace3793fe552208d4049b9ebad6a1f6c399e1a" :answer-field/choices ["q-347769/field-1/dd033485ad1b20e02b3b038ad4ace3793fe552208d4049b9ebad6a1f6c399e1a" "q-347769/field-1/d4fc5106c86c1246cb2d77e899c8c1892c146704c468558a9a4eec5c8a74d079"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347769" :question/id #uuid "8e2c57c0-a1f8-50a8-ae72-0551055de88e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347769" :question/problem "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n8-0.4+0.02-0.001+⋯.\n$$\n\n Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=8$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-0.4}{8}=-0.05.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1-(-0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1+0.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{800}{105} \\\\  & =\\frac{160}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347769/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2954b59f-d701-502f-963b-b62098a87c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353146/field-1/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" :answer/id #uuid "8f4c45c0-bf9f-5f40-a095-26d6775de861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353146/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d79b536d-ca46-5515-a75d-1a58b28eaeb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353146/field-1/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-353146/field-1/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353146" :question/id #uuid "92c6649b-02e3-53cb-8890-9951a5abc116" :question/math-academy-id "q-353146" :question/problem "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n1.5+1.2+0.96+0.768+⋯.\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=1.5$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1.2}{1.5}=0.8.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{1-0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.2} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353146/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2954b59f-d701-502f-963b-b62098a87c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
